OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FAdult social care is a broad term for
OL,7,Fservices used by people who need help
OL,8,Flooking after themselves, whether it
OL,9,Fbe due to old age, a physical or
OL,10,Flearning disability, or mental health
OL,11,Fissues.
OL,13,FThe majority of people who use adult
OL,14,Fsocial care in England are over 65.
OL,16,FTypes of support include individual
OL,17,Fassistance with dressing, making food
OL,18,For going to the toilet, or stays in
OL,19,Fnursing homes, care homes and assisted
OL,20,Fliving centres.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31304
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FHow does it work in England?
OL,8,FUnlike NHS care, social care is not
OL,9,Ffree at the point of use and high
OL,10,Fcosts sometimes mean people are forced
OL,11,Fto sell their homes to pay for what
OL,12,Fthey need.
OL,14,FHow much a person pays depends on
OL,15,Ftheir financial situation, and those
OL,16,Fwith savings worth more than #23,250
OL,17,Fare not entitled to money from the
OL,18,Flocal council - a threshold that has
OL,19,Fbeen frozen for the last 16 years.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31305
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FThe Health Foundation, a think tank
OL,7,Ffor health care for people in the UK,
OL,8,Fsaid total net expenditure on adult
OL,9,Fsocial care in England was #28.7
OL,10,Fbillion in 2024/25.
OL,12,FThe total NHS budget for the same
OL,13,Fperiod was around #200 billion.
OL,15,FPolling has shown there is a lack of
OL,16,Fawareness about how the adult care
OL,17,Fsystem works, with about a third of
OL,18,Fpeople mistakenly believing it is free
OL,19,Fat the point of need.
OL,21,FHow many people use it?
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31306
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FThere were 889,000 people receiving
OL,7,Fpublicly funded long-term care in the
OL,8,Fyear to March 2025, according to
OL,9,Fanalysis published earlier this year
OL,10,Fby the King's Fund health charity.
OL,12,FThis was made up of 576,000 over-65s,
OL,13,Fand 313,000 people aged 18`64.
OL,15,FThe King's Fund said local authorities
OL,16,Fspent similar proportions of money on
OL,17,Flong-term support for working-age
OL,18,Fadults (#11.5 billion) and older
OL,19,Fpeople (#12.0 billion) in 2024/25.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
