PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FThe most recent estimates published by
OL,7,Fthe Office for National Statistics
OL,8,F(ONS) suggest there were 279,916
OL,9,Fpeople using community care services
OL,10,Fin England in the year to the end of
OL,11,FFebruary 2023 who were state-funded,
OL,12,Fwhile 23.0% (83,844) were self-funders.
OL,14,FONS data for care homes estimates just
OL,15,Fover a third (37.0%) of care home
OL,16,Fresidents in England funded themselves.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31308
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FThe number of people aged 65 and over
OL,7,Fis projected to increase by 3.3
OL,8,Fmillion in the next 20 years, and by
OL,9,F6.5 million in the next 40 years,
OL,10,Faccording to a report from the Centre
OL,11,Ffor Ageing Better.
OL,13,FWhat could reform look like?
OL,15,FBurnham has said he wants adult social
OL,16,Fcare to operate on similar principles
OL,17,Fto the NHS and be free at the point of
OL,18,Fneed, which could be interpreted in
OL,19,Fdifferent ways.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31309
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FOne approach could be for the state to
OL,7,Fpay for all personal care, such as
OL,8,Fhelping people with eating, bathing or
OL,9,Fgoing to the bathroom, and contribute
OL,10,Ftowards the costs for these services
OL,11,Fwithin facilities like care homes.
OL,13,FAnother alternative could be to
OL,14,Fintroduce a cap on how much people can
OL,15,Fpay towards social care in their
OL,16,Flifetime and raise the financial line
OL,17,Fthat makes a person eligible for free
OL,18,Fcare.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31310
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FThis would protect people from endless
OL,7,Fbills that risk decimating their
OL,8,Fsavings, and mean that only the very
OL,9,Fwealthy fund their own support.
OL,11,FSubscribe free to our weekly
OL,12,Fnewsletter for exclusive and original
OL,13,Fcoverage from ITV News. Direct to your
OL,14,Finbox every Friday morning.
OL,16,FThe former Conservative government
OL,17,Fwanted to limit the maximum cost a
OL,18,Fperson could pay to #86,000 under a
OL,19,Fsimilar policy, but it was never
OL,20,Fimplemented.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31311
SC,0011
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FThe third option would be for the
OL,7,Fgovernment to cover all the costs of
OL,8,Fadult social care, which would be the
OL,9,Fmost expensive option.
OL,11,FBurnham is due to make a speech about
OL,12,Fhis plans on Wednesday, but is not
OL,13,Fexpected to unveil his full policy
OL,14,Fjust yet.
OL,16,FAs health secretary in 2010, he
OL,17,Fsuggested a levy to pay for the then-
OL,18,FLabour government's proposed national
OL,19,Fcare service, which would take 10% off
OL,20,Fpeople's estates after they died.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31312
SC,0012
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FThe government has said there are "no
OL,7,Fplans" to resurrect this policy, which
OL,8,Fwas previously referred to by the
OL,9,FConservatives as a "death tax".
OL,11,FHow much could reform cost?
OL,13,FIf the state covered the costs of
OL,14,Feveryone currently receiving adult
OL,15,Fsocial care services in England, an
OL,16,FNHS-style social care system would
OL,17,Fcost #18.5 billion extra a year by
OL,18,F2035, the Health Foundation estimates.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G12/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31313
SC,0013
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FThis is on top of current costs, which
OL,7,Famounted to #28.7 billion in the year
OL,8,F2024/25.
OL,10,FThe Health Foundation also estimates
OL,11,Fthat just covering the cost of all
OL,12,Fpersonal care in England be around
OL,13,F#6.5bn extra in 2026/27, before rising
OL,14,Fto around #7.5bn by 2035/36.
OL,16,FBased on estimates from the former
OL,17,FConservative government, a cap on care
OL,18,Fspending and raising the financial
OL,19,Fline could cost #0.5bn extra in 2026/
OL,20,F27, which would rise to around #4bn by
OL,21,F2035/36, the think tank said.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G13/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
