PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FWould these changes work?
OL,8,FScotland currently has a system which
OL,9,Fprovides free personal care, including
OL,10,Fday-to-day needs like hygiene,
OL,11,Fmedication and meals, for adults over
OL,12,F65 at home or in residential care. It
OL,13,Fwas introduced for people older than
OL,14,F65 initially, and extended to include
OL,15,Fall adults in 2019.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G14/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31315
SC,0015
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1785336505
OL,3,CWhat is adult social care and why does
OL,4,CAndy Burnham want to reform it?
OL,6,FBaroness Louise Casey, who headed up a
OL,7,Fcommission into social care under
OL,8,Fformer PM Keir Starmer, said there had
OL,9,Fbeen 22 attempts since 1997 at
OL,10,Freforming the sector in England and
OL,11,Fnone of which had "fixed the
OL,12,Ffoundations".
OL,14,FThe commission's first report with
OL,15,Fshort-term recommendations is expected
OL,16,Fthis autumn and the second phase,
OL,17,Fmaking long-term suggestions, was
OL,18,Fgiven a deadline of reporting by 2028.
